1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:00,782
Hi.

2
00:00:00,782 --> 00:00:07,247
Let's take a practical tour of the R3 Treatment Plan Audit Application, with you in the administrator seat.

3
00:00:07,247 --> 00:00:12,992
We'll start on the desktop, work through the tabs, and finish with the tools to use if something gets stuck.

4
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:15,000
No need to memorize the menu.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,931
We'll give each screen a job.

6
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:23,530
On your desktop, double click number one, Start I Z Clinical Notes Analyzer.

7
00:00:23,530 --> 00:00:28,353
The shortcut still has the older I Z name, but it opens this application.

8
00:00:28,353 --> 00:00:32,128
Give it a moment, then sign in with your administrator account.

9
00:00:32,128 --> 00:00:35,727
Follow any first time password or recovery prompts.

10
00:00:35,727 --> 00:00:38,757
Start each visit on Status Dashboard.

11
00:00:38,757 --> 00:00:44,766
That's your quick look at the workload: saved records, missing information, and items needing attention.

12
00:00:44,766 --> 00:00:47,608
From here, let's find one patient.

13
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:51,187
Patient Roster is your patient list.

14
00:00:51,187 --> 00:00:55,253
Use it when you're starting with a person's name or medical record number.

15
00:00:55,253 --> 00:00:58,384
That's what M R N means.

16
00:00:58,384 --> 00:01:01,528
Search, then click the matching record number.

17
00:01:01,528 --> 00:01:06,010
Patient Record Detail shows that person's information and linked plans.

18
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:10,417
Check the person, source, and location before choosing a saved plan.

19
00:01:10,417 --> 00:01:12,677
Some patients won't have a plan yet.

20
00:01:12,677 --> 00:01:15,922
The patient list and the plan list aren't the same thing.

21
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:20,989
If you're starting with a plan instead, use Treatment Plans Roster.

22
00:01:20,989 --> 00:01:28,287
Search for the plan, choose the source you want, refresh the list, or export the matching results when needed.

23
00:01:28,287 --> 00:01:31,154
Click a plan to open Treatment Plan Detail.

24
00:01:31,154 --> 00:01:37,732
This is where you inspect the selected saved version, dates, signatures, and checklist evidence.

25
00:01:37,732 --> 00:01:40,080
A status is a starting point.

26
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:45,901
Missing Data means something is missing; Overdue means a confirmed deadline has passed.

27
00:01:45,901 --> 00:01:49,739
Compare the findings with the original document before deciding.

28
00:01:50,916 --> 00:01:53,151
Have approved documents on your computer?

29
00:01:53,151 --> 00:01:55,348
Manual Upload is their doorway.

30
00:01:55,348 --> 00:02:02,002
In the lower section, Treatment-plan binder files, click Choose Files and select the documents for one plan.

31
00:02:02,002 --> 00:02:06,055
Click Upload and securely process binder, then give it a moment.

32
00:02:06,055 --> 00:02:08,542
Read the result and any warnings.

33
00:02:08,542 --> 00:02:13,542
Stored without parsing means the app couldn't read that file, even though it saved it.

34
00:02:13,542 --> 00:02:16,459
A finished upload isn't an all clear.

35
00:02:16,459 --> 00:02:20,575
Click Review in Patient Roster and inspect the saved plan.

36
00:02:20,575 --> 00:02:23,744
Only correct a patient number after checking the source.

37
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:30,363
While you're in Treatment Plan Detail, scroll to Checklist Evidence and select an item.

38
00:02:30,363 --> 00:02:40,729
As the administrator, you can approve a criterion you've verified, save a clear comment, return an item for correction, or record an override with a reason.

39
00:02:40,729 --> 00:02:43,279
Choose the action that fits the evidence.

40
00:02:43,279 --> 00:02:47,396
An override records your decision; it doesn't rewrite the source.

41
00:02:47,396 --> 00:02:52,130
Keep care level changes under review until R3 confirms that policy.

42
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:55,363
Now let's look at the tabs that keep the team working.

43
00:02:56,483 --> 00:03:02,632
Use Users when someone joins the team, needs access to a facility, or forgets a password.

44
00:03:02,632 --> 00:03:06,016
Create their account and choose the appropriate role.

45
00:03:06,016 --> 00:03:09,766
Assign the facility before assigning patients to a counselor.

46
00:03:09,766 --> 00:03:13,920
For a locked out staff member, use Reset password on their row.

47
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,352
Give each person their own account, with the access their work requires.

48
00:03:18,352 --> 00:03:21,811
For your own password, we'll use Account in a moment.

49
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:29,857
Settings is for setup and approved changes: your organization, facility timezone, and the Alleva connection.

50
00:03:29,857 --> 00:03:34,566
Use the connection details provided through R3's approved setup process.

51
00:03:34,566 --> 00:03:36,220
Don't guess at those fields.

52
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:43,417
The clinical timing values are shown here for reference; changing organization settings doesn't change treatment plan deadlines.

53
00:03:43,417 --> 00:03:47,344
Once setup is ready, there's a separate place to check the connection.

54
00:03:48,483 --> 00:03:51,665
A P I Testing Harness sounds technical.

55
00:03:51,665 --> 00:03:54,493
Think of it as the connection checking page.

56
00:03:54,493 --> 00:04:00,579
Use it during approved setup or when a connection isn't working, following R3 support's instructions.

57
00:04:00,579 --> 00:04:06,147
A successful test, or a diagnostic preview, doesn't mean records have been added.

58
00:04:06,147 --> 00:04:15,188
After connection setup and import approval, use Pull patient roster in Patient Roster, or Pull full treatment plans in Treatment Plans Roster.

59
00:04:15,188 --> 00:04:18,938
If a pull is blocked, resolve the message before continuing.

60
00:04:18,938 --> 00:04:23,862
Let a running pull finish, review its warnings, and check the resulting list.

61
00:04:25,016 --> 00:04:28,034
Forensic Logs is the app's activity history.

62
00:04:28,034 --> 00:04:33,817
Open it when you need to understand who took an action, when it happened, or whether it succeeded.

63
00:04:33,817 --> 00:04:36,998
It's useful for an audit or for tracing a problem.

64
00:04:36,998 --> 00:04:39,322
It isn't where you review clinical notes.

65
00:04:39,322 --> 00:04:42,137
That stays in the patient and plan screens.

66
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:47,740
Account, at the top right, is for your own password and recovery code.

67
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:51,705
Keep that code private; you'll need it if you forget your password.

68
00:04:51,705 --> 00:04:57,551
Help is your reference when you want a reminder of a screen, a step, or a troubleshooting tip.

69
00:04:57,551 --> 00:04:59,546
You don't need to remember this whole tour.

70
00:04:59,546 --> 00:05:01,200
That's why Help is there.

71
00:05:02,350 --> 00:05:07,767
If a list looks empty, clear the search, choose All sources, and refresh it first.

72
00:05:07,767 --> 00:05:16,845
If the app won't open or seems stuck, finish any active work, then use desktop shortcut number two, Stop I Z Clinical Notes Analyzer.

73
00:05:16,845 --> 00:05:23,726
Follow its restart prompt, or use number one, Start I Z Clinical Notes Analyzer, to open it again.

74
00:05:23,726 --> 00:05:25,115
Still having trouble?

75
00:05:25,115 --> 00:05:29,888
Number three, Collect I Z Diagnostics, creates a support report.

76
00:05:29,888 --> 00:05:33,297
Send it only through R3's approved support channel.

77
00:05:33,297 --> 00:05:38,322
Number four, Quick Assist, R3 Support, opens assisted support.

78
00:05:38,322 --> 00:05:44,787
Use it when you're working with a trusted R3 support person, and review the permission request before allowing access.

79
00:05:45,950 --> 00:05:53,955
That's the administrator's route: check the dashboard, find the record, review the plan, and use the setup and support tools when needed.

80
00:05:53,955 --> 00:05:57,604
When you're finished, click Sign out and lock your computer.

81
00:05:57,604 --> 00:06:04,788
If you also want to shut down the app itself, use desktop shortcut number two, Stop I Z Clinical Notes Analyzer.

82
00:06:04,788 --> 00:06:08,248
Signing out and stopping the app do different jobs.

83
00:06:08,248 --> 00:06:10,104
One plan at a time.

84
00:06:10,104 --> 00:06:11,733
You've got a place to start.
